{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1221406-let-s-talk-about-the-shogunate","id":1221406,"title":"Let's talk about the Shogunate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-23T00:44:14-07:00","id":1221406,"title":"Let's talk about the Shogunate","content":"This is a part of the game lore that I know almost nothing about. The book says it lasted from the Usurpation to the Great Contagion, and was basically the Warring States/Sengoku Jidai of the Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> How long did it last?<br /> Who were the major Heroes and Villains?<br /> What were the major Factions?<br /> What famous events occurred?<br /> What, if any, important changes happened in this era?<br /> Was it &quot;global&quot; or localized?<br /> and most importantly...<br /> <br /> <b>How can it affect my current game?</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T01:33:00-07:00","id":1221416,"title":"","content":"Let's talk about the Shogunate, bay-be; let's talk about you and me... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> :P<br /> <br /> Well, you know there's little firm canon on this, right? The Shogunate has some stuff in the Aspect books, but it's deliberately fragmented. Because getting players to piece together setting elements rather than having something coherent is <i>fun.</i> :P<br /> <br /> The Shogunate 'canonically' I believe lasted about 500 years? Somewhat less than that, it was brought up in another thread recently. I prefer to think it went closer to a millenium: one thousand years of rule is just a fun figure. Not much changes for the timeframe.<br /> <br /> Heroes/Villains/Factions for the Shogunate itself probably shifted a lot. It's gonna be pretty intricate about specifics, lots of independent lords and governors all manoeuvring against each other while a Shogun tries to rally them into a more unified whole. You're likely to have pro unity elements who favour a stronger role for the Blessed Isle and its bureaucracy, and separatists, who want as much independence for local lords as possible. Who is good and who is bad probably depends on both era and perspective. You can have a tyrannical shogun trying to extend his grip across the land, or a weary one who wants his squabbling children to unite to deal with something serious. All perspective.<br /> <br /> Famous Events... well, I believe Arms establishes some kinda revolt by fire elementals at one point? Beyond that, we don't know much. Which frustrates me: the Shogunate isn't supposed to be a lost era in the way the First Age was, yet we have little idea of how it shaped the map. The inspiration suggests that there was lots of internal fighting, but AFAIK we have very little information on that, even in the Aspect books. The closest thing I can remember was one Shogun getting assassinated by a youth movement loyal to his son.<br /> <br /> Important changes... well, it's the solidifying of the Dragon Blooded as the Rulers of Creation in most people's minds.It leaves a wider legacy than the Realm, and since it's centuries in the past, I imagine some people are nostalgic for it, even outside of successor states like Lookshy and Calin.,<br /> <br /> Global, but not in a unified sense. It affected everyone, but the degree and nature of that effect varied. Some areas were caught up in outright wars, others were probably managed by sleepy eyed daimyo wh Don't Want No Trouble.<br /> <br /> And the Shogunate can provide almost anything the First Age can. It was still a time of wonder, with a unified well trained Dragon Blooded host in command of marvels. Relics of a lost time, adventure sites, a historical origin for an area's political situation, all sorts of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T02:47:29-07:00","id":1221425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1221406-let-s-talk-about-the-shogunate?p=1221416#post1221416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Famous Events... well, I believe Arms establishes some kinda revolt by fire elementals at one point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhat, In the Last Days of the Shogunate, some Ifrit courts south of Dazra Province rejected Daimyo Sirisun's authority, so he commissioned an artefact for his champion, which .... didn't turn out well for him in the long run.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T04:39:33-07:00","id":1221449,"title":"","content":"It's a hassle at the moment for me to go back to my Aspect books for the specifics, but I can answer some things fairly broadly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1221406-let-s-talk-about-the-shogunate#post1221406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How long did it last?</div> </div> </div> </div>Writing on that has been inconsistent, but the current developers seem to want to stick to a figure of a bit less than 500 years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who were the major Heroes and Villains?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what you mean by &quot;major&quot;, but between the Aspect books and Arms of the Chosen, we've got examples of particular Dragon Blooded doing noteworthy things such as going into battle with Fair Folk invasions, creating exceptional works of magical art, forging powerful weapons, desperately attempting to negotiate for the cooperation of gods (and sometimes turning to demons when that doesn't work out) and engaging in strange experiments with human beings. Plus the Sidereals observing the whole situation and trying to keep things together.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the &quot;villainous&quot; side, apart from those Dragon Blooded that would be in rebellion against the government, there would have also been personalities among the aforementioned Fair Folk, gods with particularly unpleasant conditions for their service, and Third Edition can add the most extreme of the Silver Pact Lunars.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What were the major Factions?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOne of the Aspect books has a noteworthy excerpt describing how a group of generals assassinated a shogun in protest of his policy of trying to compromise with rebellious regional governors rather than bring them in line with the central administration. It's a protest rather than a coup, because the generals in question immediately surrender themselves and are prepared to commit suicide, and the policy in question is also one that the shogun's successor happens to disagree with. That's an example of a political division that might have occurred during the period.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What famous events occurred?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one particular one was a raksha breakthrough in a certain Southern city. It was a place in which Shogunate policies about water distribution had been causing tension for some time beforehand, to the point where people were openly distributing anti-establishment pamphlets, and ultimately performing reality destabilizing rituals in the streets. When the Fair Folk came through, numbering about a million, they actually had collaborators among the human population, doing things like sabotaging communication centres and skyship docking stations. The Shogunate attempts to contain the invasion were described as having extreme casualties, including more than a hundred Exalted equipped with Dragon Armour. It was described as being the largest breakthrough in a hundred years, in terms suggesting that smaller ones happened frequently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, if any, important changes happened in this era?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean within the era?<br /> <br /> \u200bHmmm... I've often inferred the presence of policies intended to bring mortal populations increasingly under the control of the Exalted and harnessing them for hard labour in an attempt to keep systems going in the absence of the First Age's magic. Also, even before the Great Contagion, economic breakdowns are periodically causing portions of the world to disintegrate entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How can it affect my current game?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bProbably mostly in cultural background for people and practices, similar to what House Tepet has (as well as unnamed cadet Houses). Perhaps occasionally as a basis for stories with which one can consider their current plans and actions. And a source of clues about where the look for Artifacts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T05:00:23-07:00","id":1221451,"title":"","content":"It's a deliberate blank spot in the time-line for the most part. We know roughly the shape of the political situation, a few curt references to events that were important at the time, and that's about it. It serves the same function for Dragonbloods as the First Age does for Solars: a golden age of lost wonders when they were united (nominally) as a political body and their rule spread over the length and breadth of Creation, before a calamity brought it crashing down. <br /> <br /> It can affect your campaign exactly as much or as little as you want. It's a source for lost manses and artifact caches that isn't the First Age. It's the historical narrative that unites and divides the Realm and Lookshy. It's when a few of the popular operas playing in the Imperial City right now are set (and/or were written). To those with no knowledge of the First Age, it <i>is</i> the mythic past. To scholars who know better, it's a hotly debated political clusterfuck. <br /> <br /> If you're a history buff and feel like fleshing it out, you could plunder the Warring States period for historical figures and events and translate them into dragonblooded feuds. That's something I'd love to see but don't have time for right now. If I ever get around to running the early-Realm dragonblooded game I've had kicking around in my head for years, I'll flesh it out for my campaign since it'll be within living memory for dragonbloods. Until then, I'm happy with it being an unconnected series of mostly local events that explain cool shit that crops up in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T09:40:16-07:00","id":1222065,"title":"","content":"I believe the writing on the history of Marama's Fell takes place in the Shogunate. In the aftermath of the Usurpation, the created races of the previous Deliberative were suspect for continued loyalty to the fallen Solars. So instead of doing something reasonable, the Shogun/ate decided that genocide was the answer. Unsurprisingly, a shadowland resulted. It sheds light on how paranoid even the victorious Dragon-Blooded were in the early Shogunate, and as for affecting current games, resolving that ancient atrocity could be key to healing a scar upon Creation that has lasted through the Time of Turmoil. <br /> <br /> It's also a pain for me to get to my books at the moment, but I'd look into Compass: North for that reference, or it might be in Bastions of the North.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T23:30:08-07:00","id":1222176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1221406-let-s-talk-about-the-shogunate?p=1222065#post1222065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also a pain for me to get to my books at the moment, but I'd look into Compass: North for that reference, or it might be in Bastions of the North.</div> </div> </div> </div>While there is some detail scattered about there, Compass: North will dirrect you to Compass: Underworld for more depth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T01:14:21-07:00","id":1222184,"title":"","content":"My favourite thing about the Shogunate is the trashy novels about the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> SHADOWS OF THE GOLDEN CHAMBER<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Taken from the classic novel The Doom of the Emperors<br /> by Lady Sennaka, proscribed under the Anathema, but<br /> now back in circulation.<br /> \u201cBut, sire,\u201d the maiden pleaded on her knees, \u201chave<br /> mercy on my brother! His folly was merely that he loved<br /> the people as he loves you. He gave from his own treasures<br /> to buy them bread only so that they might serve you with<br /> renewed devotion!\u201d<br /> The Anathema chuckled darkly from the opal throne<br /> on which he reclined and tossed a fragment of doves\u2019 liver<br /> to the leopards that crouched at his feet. An unholy light<br /> blazed around his temples, emanating from the Caste<br /> Mark that throbbed on his brow. \u201cAnd what of the<br /> people?\u201d he asked, quoting his masters in the Deliberative.<br /> \u201cWho am I to care that they should starve? Are they<br /> not honored to serve me? Should they not cast themselves<br /> bodily into the fires, if it should be my will?\u201d He<br /> bent his fearsome gaze upon the girl. \u201cAbase yourself<br /> before my throne, cringing child \u2014 your brother\u2019s fate<br /> may or may not be the torture chamber, but your fate lies<br /> in obedience to me, body and soul.\u201d<br /> The maiden Anata was young, but she had Exalted<br /> long ago, and the power of the Dragon of Fire coiled within<br /> her body and pulsed along her veins. She knew her duty to<br /> her Solar lords, but she also remembered that the place of<br /> the Exalted was to guide and protect those who were set<br /> below them in the paths of existence. As you are above<br /> them, so shall you lead them, so that, in time, they too may<br /> know the glory of the Dragons, her teachers had said. Every<br /> fiber in her body yearned to throw itself before the<br /> Anathema\u2019s feet and crawl to him in feverish obedience,<br /> but the spirit of the Dragon of Fire itself seemed to whisper<br /> in her ears and hold her back.<br /> Here, in this castle of orichalcum and ebony that<br /> floated miles above the earth below, the Anathema ruled<br /> body and soul. Their twisted sorceries drew power from the<br /> worlds of the demons and the blood of the innocent and<br /> gave them inhuman strength and unthinkable power. But in<br /> the lands below, the Dragons were speaking to their Chosen,<br /> telling them of the future that was to come.<br /> At that moment, Anata felt the might of the Dragon<br /> of Fire fill her, and she rose to her feet in fury. \u201cI am your<br /> servant, my lord, but not your slave! I will obey you, as is<br /> my sworn duty, but hear me now \u2014 if you continue in your<br /> cruelty, the day will come when the Dragons themselves<br /> will take human bodies to stand against you and cast you<br /> beyond the boundaries of Creation!\u201d<br /> The Anathema laughed coldly, and the light of his<br /> bloodstained aura danced around him as he gestured to the<br /> guards. \u201cIt seems this girl thinks that she can challenge us.<br /> Very well. Have her taken to the arena. I shall watch her<br /> perish in agony. So shall die all who dare defy our will!<br /> Unconquered Sun, may our power never fail!\u201d</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T05:36:12-07:00","id":1222216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1221406-let-s-talk-about-the-shogunate?p=1222065#post1222065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the writing on the history of Marama's Fell takes place in the Shogunate. In the aftermath of the Usurpation, the created races of the previous Deliberative were suspect for continued loyalty to the fallen Solars. So instead of doing something reasonable, the Shogun/ate decided that genocide was the answer. Unsurprisingly, a shadowland resulted. It sheds light on how paranoid even the victorious Dragon-Blooded were in the early Shogunate, and as for affecting current games, resolving that ancient atrocity could be key to healing a scar upon Creation that has lasted through the Time of Turmoil.<br /> <br /> It's also a pain for me to get to my books at the moment, but I'd look into Compass: North for that reference, or it might be in Bastions of the North.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is more to that story. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letter from Chumyo Tatenae to her Husband</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The disposal of Anathema \u201cpets\u201d and slaves has proven more complex than we originally anticipated. While it was easy enough to dispose of the obviously nonhuman ones or those who attempted to defend their masters and mistresses, we eventually found ourselves faced with problems of, to be frank, pure morality. Moral dilemmas came up when considering the unwilling slaves (or those who claimed to have been taken against their will) and the near-human beastmen who had been bred in servitude. Simply slaughtering them wholesale would have been morally reprehensible. Having the troops put them to the sword would have been setting a poor ethical precedent and creating butchers rather than warriors. We want our soldiers to kill on command, but having them slaughter innocent creatures who look mostly human and who are screaming for mercy \u2014 well, anyone can see the potential problems there.<br /> We were faced with a difficult situation, however. The battles with the Anathema had damaged a lot of arable farmland, and often, their stored food and grain had been destroyed along with their Manses or looted by the mobs, despite the military\u2019s best attempts to maintain public order. As such, releasing large numbers of slaves into the general population \u2014 especially when most of them were only trained for military or personal service and, therefore, would have been little use in farming or harvesting \u2014 was decided by our commanders to be unwise. There was also, and I admit that I had strong feelings on this point, the question of the beastmen breeding with the normal humans in the area. We managed to resolve matters to some extent. The beastmen were seconded to frontier territory garrisons, where I understand there have been some incursions by the Fair Folk. Their leaders have been given some guarantees about territory and founding their own tribes, but frankly, I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if they all die tragically with arrows in their backs. We both know how this sort of thing works out. Of the human slaves and servants, the ones who\u2019d been trained as soldiers were drafted into the army and will receive full citizenship after a decade\u2019s service. The concubines, minions and the like were divided among officers and staff with the position to warrant personal retainers. In some ways, it\u2019s the last that actually disturbs me the most. How can we guarantee that these apparently harmless servants aren\u2019t actually traps waiting to be sprung? You and I both know that the Anathema were capable of twisting a person\u2019s mind like paper between their fingers. You know better than I how many of their toys and tools have proven to be booby-trapped in some way, usually lethally. Your division\u2019s already lost several sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also in 2e canon at least Marama was an active member of Team Oblivion. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Compass Underworld</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It was becoming equally clear to the officers of Camp 17 that Commandant Marama was quite insane. Far from being concerned about the growing shadowland, Marama seemed pleased with it. Supposedly, she even told one of her subordinates that she could hear a voice from the shadowland whispering to her at night\u2014letting her know how much it loved her, singing her to sleep at night. (Or so the rumors went. The subordinate in question was summarily executed for sedition.) The Shogunate was well aware of the problems with Marama\u2019s Fell but was preoccupied with other issues in consolidating its authority. The Shogunate did draw up several long-term plans for shrinking Marama\u2019s Fell, but it was not able to enact them prior to the onset of the Great Contagion. Camp 17 had long been closed by that time, of course. Unable to neutralize the shadowland, the Shogunate instead evacuated its personnel centuries earlier once the last of the camp\u2019s inmates had been exterminated. Anjei Marama did not make it out. The commandant disappeared from the camp the day after the evacuation order was handed down, and she was never seen again by any living soul. The official inquiry stated that she had died accidentally as a result of some hazard of the shadowland.<br /> Yet widely spread rumors suggested that Marama\u2019s own subordinates had assassinated her out of disgust over her depravities. The truth is that on her last night as commandant, Marama heard an insistent whisper calling her home and she chose to answer it. She descended into the Labyrinth to offer herself to Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T06:03:56-07:00","id":1222223,"title":"","content":"I feel as though it's a bit dubious to post wholesale excerpts from some of the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T09:13:35-07:00","id":1222270,"title":"","content":"I believe 2nd edition liked to call the Shogunate the 'Low First Age' to help give the idea that the DragonBlooded had a First Age to aspire for, but it had its own problems of course. Lookshy and House Tepet are the most likely links to Shogunate cultures within the DBs.<br /> <br /> A bigger aspect i think is what this time means for Lunars. They have had little described for them, but it is this time frame that they have the biggest scope of their historical story. Without the Solars hogging spotlights and most of Creation against them, 500 years as rebels defines the Lunars strongly but gave little actual page count. Most Moonsilver artifacts and a couple of jade ones from Arms of the Chosen, if not specifically First Age or Reign of Scarlet Empress would be taken collectively from the Shogunate, and a lot of those example Eras they list i at least found decently inspiring","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T14:59:31-07:00","id":1222312,"title":"","content":"One of the interesting aspects of the Shogunate being less than 500 years long is that, the period the Dragon Blooded tend to think of as the &quot;Lost Golden Age&quot; was full of wars, political instability, and was much shorter than the Reign of the Scarlet Empress. Which is honestly kinda fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T21:43:36-07:00","id":1222348,"title":"","content":"Due to the way mortal lifespans and Dragon-blooded lifespans work, through generational anecdotes the Shogunate is simultaneously as far removed from the current setting as WW1 or the Holy Roman Empire are from current life. My Grandpa used to tell me stories about where he was when JFK was shot (I actually live in Dallas, he was actually there at the parade grounds), now imagine that was the assassination of Archduke Ferdinand, or Abraham Lincoln, or Louis XVI.<br /> <br /> With Tepet dead and the Empress missing I don't think, other than a few Lunars and Sidereals, there are any Exalts alive who experienced the Shogunate, but we are sometimes only one or two generations separated from those events. Granted there was a cataclysm or two that makes this transfusion of information from person to person a little less certain, but if you assume one or two max DB lifepans, there could be someone whose grandfather was there during the equivalent of the discovery of America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}